[{"category":"section","location":"reference/#Reference","page":"Reference","text":"","title":"Reference"},{"category":"module","location":"reference/#MPSKitPeriodic.MPSKitPeriodic","page":"Reference","text":"Extension for MPSKit.jl that adds infinite MPS/MPO types with non-trivial boundary conditions.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitPeriodic.MPSKitPeriodic"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/#MPSKitPeriodic.FQHTranslator","page":"Reference","text":"FQHTranslator <: AbstractTranslator\n\nTranslator for Fractional Quantum Hall states on a cylinder. Translates quantum numbers (sectors) across unit cell boundaries.\n\nIn the Landau gauge on a cylinder, translating by shift unit cells shifts the momentum quantum number by:     ΔP = shift * Lcell * Nparticles where L_cell (norbitals) is the number of orbitals in the unit cell, and N_particles is the particle number charge.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitPeriodic.FQHTranslator"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/#MPSKitPeriodic.InfinitePeriodicEnvironments","page":"Reference","text":"InfinitePeriodicEnvironments <: AbstractMPSEnvironments\n\nEnvironments for an infinite MPS-MPO-MPS combination. These solve the corresponding fixedpoint equations:\n\nGLsi * T_LLi = λ GLsi + 1\nT_RRi * GRsi = λ GRsi - 1\n\nwhere T_LL and T_RR are the (regularized) transfer matrix operators on a give site for AL-O-AL and AR-O-AR respectively.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitPeriodic.InfinitePeriodicEnvironments"},{"category":"type","location":"reference/#MPSKitPeriodic.InfinitePeriodicMPS","page":"Reference","text":"InfinitePeriodicMPS{A<:GenericMPSTensor,B<:MPSBondTensor} <: AbtractMPS\n\nType that represents an infinite Matrix Product State.\n\nFields\n\nAL – left-gauged MPS tensors\nAR – right-gauged MPS tensors\nAC – center-gauged MPS tensors\nC – gauge tensors\n\nNotes\n\nBy convention, we have that:\n\nAL[i] * C[i] = AC[i] = C[i-1] * AR[i]\nAL[i]' * AL[i] = 1\nAR[i] * AR[i]' = 1\n\n\n\nConstructors\n\nInfinitePeriodicMPS([f, eltype], physicalspaces::Vector{<:Union{S, CompositeSpace{S}},\n            virtualspaces::Vector{<:Union{S, CompositeSpace{S}};\n            kwargs...) where {S<:ElementarySpace}\nInfinitePeriodicMPS(As::AbstractVector{<:GenericMPSTensor}; kwargs...)\nInfinitePeriodicMPS(ALs::AbstractVector{<:GenericMPSTensor}, C₀::MPSBondTensor;\n            kwargs...)\n\nConstruct an MPS via a specification of physical and virtual spaces, or from a list of tensors As, or a list of left-gauged tensors ALs.\n\nArguments\n\nAs::AbstractVector{<:GenericMPSTensor}: vector of site tensors\nALs::AbstractVector{<:GenericMPSTensor}: vector of left-gauged site tensors\nC₀::MPSBondTensor: initial gauge tensor\nf::Function=rand: initializer function for tensor data\neltype::Type{<:Number}=ComplexF64: scalar type of tensors\nphysicalspaces::AbstractVector{<:Union{S, CompositeSpace{S}}: list of physical spaces\nvirtualspaces::AbstractVector{<:Union{S, CompositeSpace{S}}: list of virtual spaces\n\nKeywords\n\ntol: gauge fixing tolerance\nmaxiter: gauge fixing maximum iterations\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MPSKitPeriodic.InfinitePeriodicMPS"},{"category":"section","location":"index/#Index","page":"Index","text":"","title":"Index"},{"category":"section","location":"#MPSKitPeriodic.jl","page":"Home","text":"","title":"MPSKitPeriodic.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Installation","page":"Home","text":"The package is not yet registered in the Julia general registry. It can be installed trough the package manager with the following command:\n\npkg> add git@github.com:ManyBodyLab/MPSKitPeriodic.jl.git","title":"Installation"},{"category":"section","location":"#Code-Samples","page":"Home","text":"julia> using MPSKitPeriodic","title":"Code Samples"},{"category":"section","location":"#License","page":"Home","text":"MPSKitPeriodic.jl is licensed under the APL2 License). By using or interacting with this software in any way, you agree to the license of this software.\n\n\n\nThis page was generated using Literate.jl.","title":"License"}]
